The <code>PASS</code> line for Pair G1 / Pair Q1 is the strongest possible on-chain claim this BIP can make for the Phase-1 classical-security modes: every byte that the verifier consumes — <code>public_inputs</code>, <code>proof</code>, AND <code>vk</code> — was recovered from a single TX_R reveal and bound back to the matching TX_C commit by <code>SHA256d</code>; no out-of-band file or registry was consulted at any step. <code>snarkjs</code> is the canonical reference verifier for both Groth16 and PLONK proofs; an equivalent in-process <code>spvnode</code> verdict for the existing Groth16 BN254 / <code>"curve": "bn128"</code> mode can be obtained today by rebuilding libdogecoin with <code>--with-mcl</code> or <code>--with-rapidsnark</code> (which makes <code>dogecoin_zk_verify_proof</code> dispatch to the herumi/mcl or rapidsnark backend instead of returning DELEGATED). This in-process refactor is a defense-in-depth convenience for the classical mode, '''not''' the BIP's long-term growth path — the post-quantum-safe growth path runs through mode <code>0x02</code> <code>DOGECOIN_ZK_MODE_STARK_S2</code> (see "PQC-safe growth path" under Rationale) and through the already-shipping sibling Post-Quantum Signature Commitments BIP (Falcon-512 / Dilithium2 / Raccoon-G-44 in-library verifiers).

===Mainnet v2 cascade (Pair G2 Groth16 + Pair Q2 PLONK) — replay-resistant tx_binding end-to-end===

A second end-to-end cascade was broadcast on Dogecoin mainnet on 2026-05-13 to demonstrate ZKP1 v1 (vk-on-chain) ''with the Phase-1 <code>tx_binding</code> public input enabled'' for both proof systems. The only material difference from the v1 cascade above is that <code>contrib/zk_carrier/scripts/broadcast_set.sh</code> now derives <code>tx_binding == tx_base_sighash(TX_C)</code> via <code>such -c tx_sighash32</code> against the carrier-stripped base tx, threads it into <code>witness_helper.py --tx-binding-hex …</code>, and the resulting proof commits to that 248-bit binding as its 3rd public input. spvnode then recomputes the same hash from the matched TX_C bytes via <code>dogecoin_zk_compute_tx_base_sighash</code> and emits <code>[zk-commit] tx_binding match</code> immediately before <code>Reveal validated</code> — closing the cross-tx-replay window identified in the v1 deployment. Both pairs were broadcast against the same funded reference address <code>DDMpdcTrWnZT38tRMebbYzCSAgLSnVMqvr</code> (UTXO state: <code>https://chain.so/address/DOGE/DDMpdcTrWnZT38tRMebbYzCSAgLSnVMqvr</code>).

